tweets.text:
@chambleebrandel PoY debate... It's a shame that in the post-Moneyball era, stats are simply not respected. Wins are so naive and superficial when there's clearly a dominant evidence-based stats leader in the PoY race.

That said, the final 3 events will change everything, and any of these players (pictured) could grab the PoY race lead. Many of whom nobody talks about... Burns, Rory, Kim, Colin, Fox, Rai... 

Lastly, we shouldn't discount the reality that Scottie will definitely earn all the votes among stats-based voters... but (depending on the last 3 events) we could have half a dozen guys splitting the vote among 'wins' or 'moments' based voters... and the Euros may rally around Fitz (taking away votes from, say, Cam Young)... allowing Scottie to win a plurality of votes. @DataGolf @Garywilliams1Up @MattAdamsFoL @TrippIsenhourGC @AnnaJacksonGC @damonhackGC @DanHicksNBC @SmylieKaufman10

